# Theorem authority the same-origin proxy forwards to (server-side only).
THEOREM_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082
# Bearer for that authority with tenant:read|tenant:write|models:invoke scopes.
# Never commit a real value; .env is gitignored.
THEOREM_API_TOKEN=

# Sign-in. With a client id the proxy calls Theorem as the signed-in person
# instead of with THEOREM_API_TOKEN, which names no person (a static token
# cannot open a workspace on an execution host). The client is configured on
# the Theorem server in RUSTY_RED_OAUTH_CLIENTS_JSON with the redirect URI
# <this origin>/auth/callback and "extra_scopes": ["models:invoke"].
THEOREM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# Only if the server configures the client with a secret.
THEOREM_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Theorem's public URL (its OAuth issuer) when it differs from THEOREM_API_URL.
THEOREM_OAUTH_ISSUER=
# Signing in at an issuer that is not Theorem's own, such as WorkOS AuthKit:
# set THEOREM_OAUTH_ISSUER to the issuer exactly as its metadata names it (for
# AuthKit, the AuthKit domain), register <this origin>/auth/callback there as
# a redirect URI for THEOREM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID, and set the two below. Such an
# issuer names no ways in, so the sign-in page shows one button and the issuer
# asks how on its own page.
# What a sign-in asks for, space separated. Unset, it is Theorem's own scopes
# (run:read run:write models:invoke graph:read graph:write agency:approve).
# Another issuer is asked for its own, e.g. "openid profile email
# offline_access"; Theorem then decides what the person may do. The issuer
# must grant every scope listed: a session granted fewer is signed out.
# THEOREM_OAUTH_SCOPE=
# The resource tokens are bound to (their audience). Unset, it is
# <issuer>/mcp, where Theorem's own issuer serves it. With another issuer it
# is the URL registered there for Theorem, e.g. https://<theorem host>/mcp.
# THEOREM_OAUTH_RESOURCE=
# Seals the session cookie: at least 32 random characters (openssl rand -hex 32).
THEOREM_SESSION_SECRET=
# The session cookie's name, theorem_session when unset. Cookies are kept per host,
# not per port, so a second local server on localhost needs its own.
# THEOREM_SESSION_COOKIE=
